<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Ag Secretariat says prod. numbers wrong.</title>
<headline>Argentine Ag Secretariat says prod. numbers wrong.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday it issued a set of old agricultural production estimates Tuesday, giving the mistaken impression it had lowered its estimate of maize output.</p>
<p>The figures in Tuesday's press release were several months out of date, a secretariat spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Revised crop estimates are due to be announced Aug 20.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, the following set of 1996/97 crop production forecasts (in tonnes), which were issued last month, still apply:</p>
<p>    Cotton		 1,017,000</p>
<p>    Birdseed		  21,000</p>
<p>    Rice		   1,208,000</p>
<p>    Oats		     310,000</p>
<p>    Safflower		 15,000</p>
<p>    Brewers' barley	441,000</p>
<p>    Forrage barley	   4,000</p>
<p>    Rye			 36,000</p>
<p>    Rape			 4,000</p>
<p>    Sunflower seed     5,062,000</p>
<p>    Linseed		   72,000</p>
<p>    Maize		 14,699,000</p>
<p>    Peanuts		  265,000</p>
<p>    Millet		    52,000</p>
<p>    Beans		    287,000</p>
<p>    Soybeans	    11,009,000</p>
<p>    Grain sorghum	2,496,000</p>
<p>    Wheat		 15,985,000</p>
<p>    Total		 52,983,000</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
